"""B3: Hidden Binary-Grid Time Evolution.

Model (inferred from inputs, documented assumptions):
- data/initial_state.npy is an uncorrelated random +/-1 configuration on a
  100x100 square lattice (nearest-neighbour equality fractions ~0.5).
- parameters.json `control` = 2.0236 is interpreted as the temperature T in
  units J/kB = 1.  The 2D Ising critical temperature is Tc = 2/ln(1+sqrt(2))
  = 2.26918..., so T = 2.0236 is a quench below Tc: the random state coarsens
  (Ising domain growth), matching the episode identifier.
- Dynamics: nonconserved single-spin-flip Metropolis (Glauber) kinetics with
  H = -J sum_<ij> s_i s_j, J = 1, periodic boundaries.  Updates are applied on
  the two checkerboard sublattices so the sweep can be vectorised with numpy;
  this differs from random-sequential update order only in short-time
  transients, not in the asymptotic coarsening exponent.
- Time is measured in full-lattice Monte Carlo sweeps; snapshot_times and
  measurement_times are sweep counts.  One RNG stream:
  numpy.random.default_rng(dynamics_seed), created exactly once.

Observed behaviour (measured in this run): at T = 2.0236 the finite
100x100 system coarsens for t <~ 500 sweeps and then equilibrates into the
ordered phase (|m| -> ~0.90 ~ Onsager m_eq = 0.912; wall density -> plateau
rho_eq ~ 0.069 set by equilibrium thermal droplets).  Later times are
equilibrium fluctuations, not coarsening.

Diagnostics (documented conventions, also written into the JSON notes):
- seriesA row 0: per-site energy e = -(1/N) sum_<ij> s_i s_j (bonds once).
  seriesA row 1: magnetisation m = (1/N) sum s_i.
- seriesB row 0: domain length L(t) = 1/rho(t) (inverse domain-wall density);
  tracks the growing domain size during coarsening and saturates at
  1/rho_eq after equilibration.  seriesB row 1: wall density rho(t)
  = fraction of unlike nearest-neighbour pairs (axes averaged).
- stackC: C(r,t) = <s(x) s(x+r)> averaged over all displacement vectors with
  |r| in [r-0.5, r+0.5) (circular/periodic), r = 0..max_r-1, per snapshot.
- stackD: column-averaged magnetisation profile m(x) per snapshot.
- stackE: per snapshot, row 0 = column-averaged +1-phase density,
  row 1 = column-averaged -1-phase density.
- Coarsening window (data-driven): measurement times from the first sample
  until rho(t) first falls within 2% of its late-time plateau (median over
  the last 10% of samples).
- metadataA: Family-Vicsek collapse of the connected, normalised correlation
  y = (C - m^2)/(1 - m^2) vs x = r/L(t), restricted to snapshots inside the
  coarsening window (equilibrated snapshots have C ~ m^2 and cannot collapse).
  collapse_relative_rms_spread = RMS(y_i(x) - master(x)) / RMS(master(x))
  over the common overlap grid x in [0, min_i((r_max-1)/L_i)] (200-point
  grid, linear interpolation); collapse_quality = clip(1 - rel_rms, 0, 1).
- metadataB: log-log OLS fit L(t) = A t^alpha over the coarsening window.
"""

import json
import os

import numpy as np
from scipy.stats import linregress
# matplotlib is imported lazily inside main() (with a numpy-only fallback
# figure renderer used when matplotlib is unavailable in the runtime).

DATA_DIR = "data"
